---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
	title="Bicycle-Theft Partnerships | Bait Bikes"
	description="A partnership model for law enforcement, cities, counties, states, bike shops, campuses, transit, insurers, and manufacturers."
	kicker="Partners"
>
	<header class="page-hero shell">
		<p class="eyebrow">No single institution sees the whole route</p>
		<h1>Connect the people who sell, secure, report, investigate, and recover bikes.</h1>
		<p class="lede">Bike shops see suspicious repairs and resale. Campuses and transit systems see concentrated theft. Cities control racks and public space. Manufacturers know product identity. Agencies see reports and repeat contacts. Partnership turns those fragments into prevention.</p>
		<nav class="page-nav" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#institutions">Institutions</a><a href="#agency-onboarding">Agency onboarding</a><a href="#manufacturers">Manufacturers</a><a href="#start">Start</a></nav>
	</header>

	<section class="section" id="institutions">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">A regional table</p><h2>Give every partner a bounded role.</h2></div><p>The goal is not one enormous surveillance database. It is a documented way to exchange the minimum information needed for prevention, reporting, recovery, investigation, and lawful prosecution.</p></div>
			<div class="card-grid">
				<article class="card"><span class="number">LAW ENFORCEMENT</span><h3>Local, county, state, and regional</h3><p>Align reporting, case routing, bait-asset policy, dispatch, evidence, fencing investigations, prosecutor coordination, and cross-jurisdiction referrals.</p></article>
				<article class="card"><span class="number">PUBLIC REALM</span><h3>Cities, transit, campuses, parks</h3><p>Improve parking design, lighting, anchors, signage, registration, incident reporting, camera governance, hotspot analysis, and communication with riders.</p></article>
				<article class="card"><span class="number">BIKE ECONOMY</span><h3>Shops, rentals, fleets, insurers</h3><p>Verify ownership, record serials and components, recognize suspicious transactions, preserve evidence, support recovery, and strengthen customer education.</p></article>
				<article class="card"><span class="number">PRODUCT</span><h3>Manufacturers and component makers</h3><p>Build durable identity, secure tracking, ownership transfer, service authorization, tamper awareness, software support, and privacy-respecting recovery exports.</p></article>
				<article class="card"><span class="number">JUSTICE</span><h3>Prosecutors and counsel</h3><p>Clarify charging thresholds, surveillance and retention rules, disclosure, evidence foundations, interagency agreements, and the boundaries of lawful operations.</p></article>
				<article class="card"><span class="number">COMMUNITY</span><h3>Riders and advocates</h3><p>Define real harms, review policy, improve accessibility and language, identify reporting barriers, evaluate equity, and hold programs accountable.</p></article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section light" id="agency-onboarding">
		<div class="shell split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Agency and institution onboarding</p><h2>Begin with a 30-day problem definition.</h2>
				<div class="steps">
					<article class="step"><div><h3>Name an accountable owner</h3><p>Identify operational, legal, evidence, technology, public-information, and community-review contacts.</p></div></article>
					<article class="step"><div><h3>Build the baseline</h3><p>Review at least a year of theft, attempted theft, recovery, location, value, lock, serial, and disposition data with known reporting limitations.</p></div></article>
					<article class="step"><div><h3>Map partners and gaps</h3><p>Document how reports, owner records, shop observations, video, tracker events, and cross-jurisdiction leads currently move—or fail to move.</p></div></article>
					<article class="step"><div><h3>Select a bounded intervention</h3><p>Choose prevention, infrastructure, registration, focused outreach, bait-bike deployment, fencing investigation, or a measured combination.</p></div></article>
					<article class="step"><div><h3>Publish the safeguards</h3><p>Explain authority, placement principles, data handling, retention, prohibited uses, contact policy, evaluation, complaints, and public reporting.</p></div></article>
				</div>
			</div>
			<aside class="aside-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Starter packet</p><ul><li>Problem statement and baseline</li><li>Partner and data-flow map</li><li>Legal/policy review checklist</li><li>Asset and tracker inventory</li><li>Deployment and disengagement plan</li><li>Evidence and disclosure plan</li><li>Community and equity review</li><li>Measurement and after-action template</li></ul></aside>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" id="manufacturers">
		<div class="shell callout">
			<p class="eyebrow">Manufacturer partnership</p>
			<h2>Give every new bicycle a secure recovery path.</h2>
			<p>Work with agencies, shops, and riders before freezing the hardware. Define ownership at sale, service and rental modes, secure transfer, lost and stolen states, law-enforcement sharing, unwanted-tracking prevention, firmware support, end-of-life, and what continues working when a cloud service is unavailable.</p>
			<div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/technology/">Review the technology architecture</a><a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Contact the project</a></div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section light" id="start">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Start a partnership</p><h2>Bring a defined problem, not a predetermined tool.</h2></div><p>Tell us which institution you represent, the geography, the theft pattern you can document, the partners already involved, and the safeguards or technology questions you need to resolve.</p></div>
			<div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Open a partnership conversation</a><a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/bait-bikes">Explore the open organization surface</a></div>
		</div>
	</section>
</SiteLayout>
